1
00:00:12,708 --> 00:00:15,938
(Jung Yong Hwa)

2
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:18,938
(Hong Seung Hee)

3
00:00:19,008 --> 00:00:22,248
(Lee Yi Kyung)

4
00:00:23,348 --> 00:00:25,318
(Park Yu Na)

5
00:00:36,598 --> 00:00:39,968
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:40,028 --> 00:00:41,328
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:42,998
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:01:05,888 --> 00:01:08,888
(Juan Hospital)

9
00:01:18,198 --> 00:01:22,638
Man, Director Kim chewed me out for reusing these clothes again.

10
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:24,178
Throw this away.

11
00:01:24,238 --> 00:01:25,708
- Clean this up quickly.
- Yes.

12
00:01:28,808 --> 00:01:30,478
Excuse me, are you throwing this away?

13
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,218
- Pardon?
- If you are throwing it away,

14
00:01:32,218 --> 00:01:33,518
could I wear it...

15
00:01:33,588 --> 00:01:34,988
Sure, go ahead.

16
00:01:35,048 --> 00:01:36,048
Thank you.

17
00:01:39,428 --> 00:01:40,458
Hey!

18
00:01:47,928 --> 00:01:49,738
Get him.

19
00:01:49,798 --> 00:01:52,298
We are in front of a hospital. Did no one teach you any manners?

20
00:01:52,368 --> 00:01:54,238
Keep the weapons in the factory.

21
00:01:55,668 --> 00:01:58,008
Hey, get him. I said get him.

22
00:01:59,508 --> 00:02:00,508
What?

23
00:02:01,548 --> 00:02:02,548
Where did my ring go?

24
00:02:04,548 --> 00:02:08,218
That is what you get for smashing my guys with your own hands. Get him.

25
00:02:08,288 --> 00:02:09,958
Wait.

26
00:02:10,018 --> 00:02:11,758
- Where did it go?
- Why is he getting up? Why?

27
00:02:13,088 --> 00:02:14,088
What is wrong with him?

28
00:02:14,158 --> 00:02:15,558
(Juan Hospital)

29
00:02:15,628 --> 00:02:18,228
- Get him.
- No, I mean...

30
00:02:18,298 --> 00:02:20,068
Where did it go?

31
00:02:20,128 --> 00:02:22,568
- Are you kidding me? Hey. Get him.
- Son of a...

32
00:02:22,628 --> 00:02:24,298
Hey, get him. Hey, hold still. Stay right there.

33
00:02:24,368 --> 00:02:25,368
Come here.

34
00:02:41,148 --> 00:02:42,148
I told you, right?

35
00:02:44,088 --> 00:02:45,088
That I would always...

36
00:02:46,988 --> 00:02:48,128
protect you.

37
00:02:51,928 --> 00:02:55,728
Cut. What is going on? Hey. Who are you? Darn it.

38
00:02:57,198 --> 00:02:59,768
Who are you? Can you not see we are filming?

39
00:02:59,838 --> 00:03:03,938
Who do you think you are, barging onto my set and ruining everything?

40
00:03:04,008 --> 00:03:05,508
What is he saying?

41
00:03:05,578 --> 00:03:07,478
Hey, are you okay? Your hands? Your head?

42
00:03:07,548 --> 00:03:08,908
Is everything intact?

43
00:03:08,978 --> 00:03:12,988
- Who are you?
- Hey, is she someone you know?

44
00:03:13,048 --> 00:03:14,318
No, she is not.

45
00:03:14,388 --> 00:03:15,388
Did you hurt your head?

46
00:03:15,448 --> 00:03:18,458
I told you, right? Never go around alone.

47
00:03:18,518 --> 00:03:22,128
You cannot even eat alone. You might get attacked like earlier.

48
00:03:22,188 --> 00:03:23,798
When did I get attacked?

49
00:03:27,928 --> 00:03:29,198
- Wait.
- What is wrong with you?

50
00:03:29,268 --> 00:03:31,298
Have we met before...

51
00:03:32,738 --> 00:03:35,338
I have definitely seen those eyes before.

52
00:03:37,538 --> 00:03:40,108
What do you mean, seen those eyes before?

53
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:43,148
You see this face every day, so why would only these eyes be unfamiliar?

54
00:03:43,218 --> 00:03:46,618
Did you just hit me? Are you crazy? What is your deal? Who are you?

55
00:03:46,688 --> 00:03:48,548
What is wrong with you? Are you asking without knowing?

56
00:03:48,618 --> 00:03:49,618
I know your secret...

57
00:03:54,088 --> 00:03:56,598
How many times do I tell you? Ears were made to hold glasses...

58
00:03:56,658 --> 00:03:58,098
What? What did you do with your glasses?

59
00:03:59,668 --> 00:04:02,768
Whatever. It is dangerous to go around alone.

60
00:04:02,828 --> 00:04:05,338
What will you do if you get threatened again?

61
00:04:05,398 --> 00:04:07,008
Threatened? Is she an anti-fan?

62
00:04:12,038 --> 00:04:13,848
Okay, okay.

63
00:04:13,848 --> 00:04:17,248
I see. So,

64
00:04:17,318 --> 00:04:19,248
you are a die-hard fan of mine.

65
00:04:19,318 --> 00:04:20,918
You saw the action scene and got worried.

66
00:04:20,988 --> 00:04:23,058
Always worrying if I will get sick or hurt,

67
00:04:23,118 --> 00:04:25,488
my dedicated fan club.

68
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:28,158
Pathetic Um-ppo?

69
00:04:29,698 --> 00:04:31,498
Gosh, what is he talking about?

70
00:04:31,558 --> 00:04:33,128
Look at me, are you sure you are not hurt anywhere?

71
00:04:34,998 --> 00:04:36,468
What is going on here?

72
00:04:36,538 --> 00:04:38,268
Are those two in some sort of relationship?

73
00:04:38,338 --> 00:04:40,038
What? No, they are not.

74
00:04:40,108 --> 00:04:42,838
Then why did she come to my set? What in the world?

75
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:45,278
Is that not the costume we use for our shoot?

76
00:04:45,338 --> 00:04:48,978
Who gave them permission to wear it? Hey.

77
00:04:49,048 --> 00:04:50,218
Take that off of them right now.

78
00:04:50,278 --> 00:04:51,748
- What?
- Strip it all off.

79
00:04:51,818 --> 00:04:52,818
Wait a minute.

80
00:04:52,878 --> 00:04:53,988
Drag them out and take it off right now.

81
00:04:54,048 --> 00:04:55,048
I will not take it off.

82
00:04:55,048 --> 00:04:56,518
- I cannot take it off.
- Drag them out.

83
00:04:59,218 --> 00:05:00,228
What is going on?

84
00:05:05,358 --> 00:05:07,498
(Oh! My Guard)

85
00:05:07,568 --> 00:05:10,068
(Episode 2)

86
00:05:11,538 --> 00:05:13,568
What was up with that girl earlier?

87
00:05:13,638 --> 00:05:16,168
What kind of fan is that aggressive?

88
00:05:16,238 --> 00:05:18,508
I have definitely seen her somewhere.

89
00:05:22,778 --> 00:05:25,148
That extra.

90
00:05:26,248 --> 00:05:28,018
Then...

91
00:05:28,088 --> 00:05:30,618
Does that woman have my ring?

92
00:05:36,058 --> 00:05:37,758
Good thing there were more clothes to toss.

93
00:05:37,758 --> 00:05:39,158
I was almost in big trouble.

94
00:05:40,528 --> 00:05:42,928
Oh man, but where did he run off to in the meantime?

95
00:05:44,898 --> 00:05:47,838
Still, it is a relief. He does not seem to be hurt anywhere.

96
00:05:53,408 --> 00:05:55,548
Actually, when the time of death was pronounced,

97
00:05:55,608 --> 00:05:58,878
I think I saw the patient's hand move for a moment.

98
00:05:59,948 --> 00:06:00,948
I am sorry.

99
00:06:01,018 --> 00:06:02,688
Excuse me, please take a look at this.

100
00:06:07,988 --> 00:06:09,028
The young lady is really alive.

101
00:06:13,028 --> 00:06:14,198
She is perfectly alive and well.

102
00:06:14,268 --> 00:06:16,168
I checked the security cameras myself.

103
00:06:20,138 --> 00:06:22,338
You should file a missing person report right away.

104
00:06:22,408 --> 00:06:24,808
We cannot do that. Find Hae Ra quietly.

105
00:06:29,348 --> 00:06:31,448
The new director coming to the Strategic Planning Team tomorrow.

106
00:06:31,518 --> 00:06:34,418
An exceptional recruitment the board agreed upon.

107
00:06:34,488 --> 00:06:37,088
Whether we use him as an ally or drive him out as an enemy,

108
00:06:37,158 --> 00:06:39,688
well, we will find out soon enough.

109
00:06:39,758 --> 00:06:40,758
You may leave.

110
00:06:54,538 --> 00:06:56,708
Oh, it is cold.

111
00:06:56,778 --> 00:07:00,408
Han Jung Woo, you really want to end up in a coffin, do you not?

112
00:07:00,478 --> 00:07:02,678
Just wait until I catch you.

113
00:07:02,748 --> 00:07:05,918
No. I should barge in right now and just...

114
00:07:05,978 --> 00:07:07,348
Wait.

115
00:07:07,418 --> 00:07:08,818
Where was Han Jung Woo's house again?

116
00:07:10,018 --> 00:07:11,358
His phone number?

117
00:07:11,418 --> 00:07:13,888
More importantly, why did I do that at the hospital earlier...

118
00:07:31,138 --> 00:07:33,148
What? Why are the brakes acting like this?

119
00:07:34,148 --> 00:07:35,578
What?

120
00:07:35,648 --> 00:07:37,078
Did someone do this on purpose again...

121
00:07:37,148 --> 00:07:38,218
Are we going to die now?

122
00:07:39,218 --> 00:07:40,588
Who says we are going to die?

123
00:07:40,648 --> 00:07:42,948
You are overestimating the top speed of a scooter.

124
00:07:43,018 --> 00:07:44,818
Because I only ever ride in cars with the highest top speeds.

125
00:07:44,888 --> 00:07:47,058
Then why did that amazing car of yours break down?

126
00:07:47,128 --> 00:07:50,328
I promise you. You are absolutely not going to die today.

127
00:07:50,398 --> 00:07:52,298
Now I am going to crash into that street tree and stop.

128
00:07:52,358 --> 00:07:53,368
You trust me, right?

129
00:08:02,108 --> 00:08:06,078
So that is why I woke up at the hospital back then.

130
00:08:07,378 --> 00:08:09,608
But why did Han Jung Woo run away earlier?

131
00:08:11,418 --> 00:08:14,888
Whatever. Let me just find that jerk's house first.

132
00:08:17,988 --> 00:08:20,558
But why can I not remember anything?

133
00:08:41,778 --> 00:08:42,948
I am starving to death.

134
00:08:45,048 --> 00:08:46,048
What?

135
00:08:50,088 --> 00:08:51,518
Yes.

136
00:08:55,828 --> 00:08:57,598
This woman looks perfectly normal,

137
00:08:57,658 --> 00:08:58,758
but are you trying to scam me right now?

138
00:08:59,758 --> 00:09:01,168
(10 Dollars)

139
00:09:01,228 --> 00:09:02,898
(Free Dried Snacks With Alcohol Orders)

140
00:09:04,638 --> 00:09:08,168
Oh my, since when did this face on the bill...

141
00:09:08,238 --> 00:09:11,678
start smiling so much?

142
00:09:11,738 --> 00:09:14,278
These fakes are rolling around all over the streets everywhere.

143
00:09:14,348 --> 00:09:17,278
This cannot be your first time. I will report the dine-and-dash,

144
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:19,118
so let us see if you can still say that in front of the police.

145
00:09:19,178 --> 00:09:21,418
- What?
- How much is everything she ate?

146
00:09:28,358 --> 00:09:30,528
(Come Again Dumplings)

147
00:09:30,598 --> 00:09:33,158
Oh, I guess all the strange things that happened today...

148
00:09:33,228 --> 00:09:35,868
were just leading up to me meeting a saviour like you.

149
00:09:37,038 --> 00:09:39,938
But since you are helping me, could you spare ten more dollars...

150
00:09:44,678 --> 00:09:46,508
Then what are you going to give me?

151
00:09:47,778 --> 00:09:49,648
You have not shown any honesty or remorse,

152
00:09:49,708 --> 00:09:50,778
so I doubt you can give me those.

153
00:09:52,118 --> 00:09:53,748
Oh, I really thought it was real money...

154
00:09:55,818 --> 00:09:58,388
Wow, you are treating me like a...

155
00:10:00,788 --> 00:10:02,688
For your kindness today,

156
00:10:02,688 --> 00:10:08,728
I will definitely repay you when we meet again someday.

157
00:10:08,798 --> 00:10:11,398
Well then, goodbye.

158
00:10:18,838 --> 00:10:21,508
Oh, man. I almost stepped on it.

159
00:10:25,548 --> 00:10:27,148
Flowers bloom even in places like this.

160
00:10:39,628 --> 00:10:43,468
Now, this is your Iron Man suit.

161
00:10:49,408 --> 00:10:50,478
Excuse me, wait a minute.

162
00:10:57,018 --> 00:11:00,188
Leave something with me instead. Like collateral?

163
00:11:03,458 --> 00:11:06,018
- That ring should do.
- I do not wear rings...

164
00:11:08,188 --> 00:11:10,228
I am wearing one. A ring?

165
00:11:10,298 --> 00:11:13,368
I was so busy eating earlier that I did not know I had this.

166
00:11:13,428 --> 00:11:15,468
Why? Is there a problem?

167
00:11:23,138 --> 00:11:24,978
Is this the American style?

168
00:11:25,038 --> 00:11:27,078
You have a strong sense of give and take.

169
00:11:29,908 --> 00:11:30,978
British style.

170
00:11:32,978 --> 00:11:34,218
I just got back from the United Kingdom today.

171
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:40,658
By the way,

172
00:11:41,828 --> 00:11:42,828
did you run away from home?

173
00:11:44,698 --> 00:11:48,128
Well, I feel more like becoming a monk than running away.

174
00:11:48,198 --> 00:11:49,928
My employer suddenly ignored me...

175
00:11:51,938 --> 00:11:54,938
Oh, I was a live-in bodyguard.

176
00:11:55,008 --> 00:11:57,508
Anyway, I have to go find that guy's house now, so...

177
00:12:00,378 --> 00:12:03,578
Then you can get this ring back here at this time tomorrow.

178
00:12:04,748 --> 00:12:06,218
Yes, see you.

179
00:12:13,528 --> 00:12:15,488
I just said that, but she actually left it.

180
00:12:16,828 --> 00:12:18,898
Is there a sauna around here...

181
00:12:24,698 --> 00:12:25,698
This way.

182
00:12:31,238 --> 00:12:32,238
What about over there?

183
00:12:33,678 --> 00:12:34,708
Keep looking.

184
00:12:39,918 --> 00:12:41,448
I do not think I walked that much,

185
00:12:41,518 --> 00:12:45,158
but why do I feel like I am losing muscle mass?

186
00:12:54,798 --> 00:12:55,928
(Waiting Line)

187
00:12:55,998 --> 00:12:57,138
Come here, stand right there.

188
00:12:57,198 --> 00:12:58,868
Keep your buttocks tight and stand still.

189
00:12:58,938 --> 00:12:59,968
If you let your guard down for a second,

190
00:13:00,038 --> 00:13:01,508
it is two laps around the parade ground.

191
00:13:04,178 --> 00:13:06,108
Am I right?

192
00:13:06,178 --> 00:13:09,708
V? Or Jung Kook?

193
00:13:09,778 --> 00:13:11,718
I am...

194
00:13:11,778 --> 00:13:15,818
Rolling Park Ji Min. What do I do?

195
00:13:15,888 --> 00:13:19,118
God, Buddha, ancestors. Please help me...

196
00:13:19,188 --> 00:13:21,558
get my hands on BTS's new album.

197
00:13:22,688 --> 00:13:24,528
Why do you have that look on your face?

198
00:13:24,598 --> 00:13:27,598
Are you not an Army? I purple you.

199
00:13:29,068 --> 00:13:30,198
I am not.

200
00:13:32,238 --> 00:13:33,668
But this is really fascinating.

201
00:13:33,738 --> 00:13:35,238
I have only seen this kind of thing on television.

202
00:13:35,308 --> 00:13:39,108
Fascinating, right? Yes, it is. I find you more fascinating.

203
00:13:40,108 --> 00:13:41,748
Have you never fangirled over an idol?

204
00:13:44,118 --> 00:13:45,148
What about an actor?

205
00:13:47,648 --> 00:13:51,418
You, what do you live for?

206
00:13:51,488 --> 00:13:52,618
Sit down here.

207
00:13:55,258 --> 00:13:57,258
(Waiting Line)

208
00:14:00,868 --> 00:14:02,968
First of all, as for actors,

209
00:14:04,038 --> 00:14:07,808
Um Tae Bong is my absolute favourite.

210
00:14:07,868 --> 00:14:11,278
Even though he has been breaking my heart a little lately.

211
00:14:12,778 --> 00:14:15,208
Um Tae Bong? What about him?

212
00:14:15,278 --> 00:14:17,848
He got caught up in another dating rumour.

213
00:14:17,918 --> 00:14:19,678
I wonder how long this one will last.

214
00:14:19,748 --> 00:14:22,288
Anyway, it is quite a mystery.

215
00:14:24,288 --> 00:14:27,058
Look. This Um Tae Bong...

216
00:14:27,128 --> 00:14:29,488
never shoots kiss scenes, you know.

217
00:14:29,558 --> 00:14:31,998
Whether it is out of loyalty to his real girlfriend...

218
00:14:32,058 --> 00:14:34,298
or if there is some other reason.

219
00:14:42,338 --> 00:14:45,138
But why are you wandering around so late at night?

220
00:14:46,678 --> 00:14:47,948
To catch some guy.

221
00:14:48,008 --> 00:14:51,178
I cannot remember where that jerk lives,

222
00:14:51,248 --> 00:14:53,848
but I do remember his company.

223
00:14:53,918 --> 00:14:57,358
It was a car company that started with a B or something.

224
00:14:58,618 --> 00:15:00,758
That would be BK Motors.

225
00:15:00,828 --> 00:15:02,088
The really big building.

226
00:15:03,358 --> 00:15:05,658
BK Motors.

227
00:15:05,728 --> 00:15:06,828
(BK Motor Group)

228
00:15:16,238 --> 00:15:17,608
Look at the state of you.

229
00:15:18,878 --> 00:15:21,948
- What department are you even in?
- My luggage has not arrived yet.

230
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:24,418
- Is it your first day?
- Yes.

231
00:15:24,478 --> 00:15:25,978
Newbies these days have no discipline.

232
00:15:29,088 --> 00:15:32,818
I am Na Dae Seong, the real power of the Strategic Planning Team.

233
00:15:32,888 --> 00:15:33,888
Right, I am...

234
00:15:33,958 --> 00:15:36,488
Anyway, stay out of our director's sight.

235
00:15:36,558 --> 00:15:39,198
He is the type to judge the hierarchy by how you dress,

236
00:15:39,258 --> 00:15:42,668
and he values team unity. Got it?

237
00:15:42,728 --> 00:15:43,738
Right.

238
00:15:49,668 --> 00:15:50,678
What are you doing?

239
00:15:52,008 --> 00:15:53,008
Follow me.

240
00:15:54,178 --> 00:15:56,748
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

241
00:15:58,318 --> 00:15:59,778
- Hi.
- Director, you are here?

242
00:16:00,888 --> 00:16:01,888
Yes.

243
00:16:03,018 --> 00:16:05,618
Everyone, our new director is here.

244
00:16:05,688 --> 00:16:08,388
I look forward to working with you. I am Director Han Jung Woo.

245
00:16:08,458 --> 00:16:09,458
What?

246
00:16:09,528 --> 00:16:10,758
We look forward to working with you, Director Han.

247
00:16:10,828 --> 00:16:12,498
(Strategic Planning Team)

248
00:16:14,328 --> 00:16:16,828
So, could someone give me an update on today's...

249
00:16:18,538 --> 00:16:19,768
Last year's BK business status report,

250
00:16:19,838 --> 00:16:20,838
the statement of financial position,

251
00:16:20,908 --> 00:16:23,008
and the list of candidates for the new model being released.

252
00:16:23,068 --> 00:16:25,838
I stayed up all night preparing every single word.

253
00:16:25,908 --> 00:16:28,278
My esteemed Director Han.

254
00:16:28,348 --> 00:16:29,348
Thank you.

255
00:16:30,718 --> 00:16:31,718
Thanks to you, I also learned about...

256
00:16:31,778 --> 00:16:33,478
my own fashion philosophy that I was unaware of.

257
00:16:34,588 --> 00:16:37,018
- Where is my office?
- It is right this way.

258
00:16:37,088 --> 00:16:39,558
Welcome.

259
00:16:42,028 --> 00:16:43,388
The actor who got hurt yesterday...

260
00:16:43,458 --> 00:16:44,558
is throwing a fit and threatening to sue.

261
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:46,898
He claims you and your fan conspired to beat him up.

262
00:16:46,958 --> 00:16:48,898
He is demanding you bring her to apologize.

263
00:16:48,968 --> 00:16:51,168
Who is this fan? What kind of fan is she?

264
00:16:51,238 --> 00:16:55,168
